\p{\strong{Std on the JVM launcher, measured again.} In the window above Std is +4.4 \% for variant A (three rounds 0.900 to 0.936 s against 0.875 to 0.891 s), above the limit of 3 \%, as it was for the first candidate in section 9.2. So that cell was measured again when nothing else of this package was running: one window, Std only, \strong{six} interleaved rounds of base, A and B.}

\table{
\tr{\th{Std, JVM launcher, six rounds}\th{Cell}\th{Rounds}\th{CPU of a pass}\th{Peak resident set}}
